      "problem": "What number is $30\\%$ less than $120$?",
      "worked_solution": "To find a number $30\\%$ *less than* $120,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% - 30\\% = 70\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n70\\% = \\dfrac{70}{100} = 0.7\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $70\\%$ of $120,$ we multiply $120$ by $0.7{:}$\n\n$$\n0.7 \\cdot 120 = 84\n$$",
